'''''Myosotis alpestris''''', the '''alpine forget-me-not''', is a [[herbaceous]] [[perennial plant]] in the [[flowering plant]] family [[Boraginaceae]]. The alpine forget-me-not is the [[County flowers of the United Kingdom|county flower]] of [[Westmorland]] in the United Kingdom.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://abcounties.com/counties/county-profiles/westmorland2/ |title=County profile for Westmorland |publisher=The Association of British Counties |access-date=17 March 2024 }}</ref>

==Distribution==
Its native distribution includes much of western, southern and central Europe and the Caucasus, east to central Asia.<ref name=powo>{{cite web |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:118892-1 |title=''Myosotis alpestris'' F.W.Schmidt |work =Plants of the World Online |publisher=Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew |access-date=17 March 2024 }}</ref> In Great Britain it occurs in only two localities, in limestone grassland in the [[North Pennines]], and at high elevation on [[mica schist]] on and nearby [[Ben Lawers]].<ref name=BSBI_Atlas2020>{{cite web |title=''Myosotis alpestris'' F.W.Schmidt |work=BSBI Online Plant Atlas 2020 |editor1=P.A. Stroh |editor2=T. A. Humphrey |editor3=R.J. Burkmar |editor4=O.L. Pescott |editor5=D.B. Roy |editor6=K.J. Walker |publisher=Botanical Society of Britain and Ireland |date=2020 |url=https://plantatlas2020.org/atlas/2cd4p9h.ht8 |access-date=17 March 2024 }}</ref>

==Taxonomy==
Four [[subspecies]] are accepted:<ref name=powo/>
*''Myosotis alpestris'' subsp. ''alpestris'' — throughout the range of the species
*''Myosotis alpestris'' subsp. ''mrkvickana'' (Velen.) Strid — North Macedonia to northern Greece
*''Myosotis alpestris'' subsp. ''pyrenaica'' (Douin) Litard. — Pyrenees
*''Myosotis alpestris'' subsp. ''suaveolens'' (Waldst. & Kit. ex Willd.) Strid — Balkan Peninsula

A former subspecies ''Myosotis alpestris'' subsp. ''asiatica'', native to Asia and northwestern North America, is now treated as a separate species, ''[[Myosotis asiatica]]'' (Vestergr.) Schischk. & Serg.<ref name="powo2">{{cite web |title=''Myosotis alpestris'' subsp. ''asiatica'' Vestergr. |website=Plants of the World Online |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:2377002-4 |access-date=2026-09-03}}</ref><ref name="usda">{{cite web |title=''Myosotis asiatica'' (Vesterg.) Schischkin & Sergievskaja: synonyms |website=USDA Plants Database |url=https://plants.sc.egov.usda.gov/plant-profile/MYAS2/synonyms |access-date=2026-09-03}}</ref>

